# `uv run --with <tool>` writes a lockfile for the ad-hoc environment it
# builds. This project does not resolve through uv -- CI installs the compiled,
# hash-pinned sets under requirements/ci/ -- so a uv.lock here is a local
# artifact, not a dependency source. Committing one adds a file no gate governs
# and breaks the manifest check, which compares the sdist against VCS.
uv.lock

